course: dictionary
lesson: 16005
title: Valuation: how much something is worth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A valuation is an expert's decision about how much money something is worth. The word comes from value, so when you see valuation, think "the worth someone has worked out". «The surveyor looked at the house and gave it a valuation of £250,000.» The surveyor is the expert, and the £250,000 is what the house is worth.
explain: Valuation can also mean how much you think something or someone is worth in a general way. «Her kindness gives her a high valuation in our class.» Nobody wrote down a price here. It means the class thinks she is very valuable to them.
explain: A valuation is not always the same as a price. «The antique expert gave the old vase a valuation of £400, but it was sold for £250.» The price is what someone paid. The valuation is the expert's view of what it is worth, and the two numbers can be different.
fact: A valuation is a decision about how much something is worth.
fact: «Valuation» comes from the word value.
fact: A surveyor makes a valuation before a house is sold or before a mortgage is given.
fact: An antique expert can give a valuation of an old vase or an old watch.
fact: In maths word problems, a valuation is a number of pounds or dollars that something is worth, not what it was sold for.
exercise: «The surveyor made a valuation of the flat.» What is a valuation? | A map of the street | *An expert's decision about how much the flat is worth | A kind of paint | A list of the people who live in the flat
exercise: Valuation comes from which word? | volunteer | *value | vacation
exercise: «The antique expert gave the old vase a valuation of £400, but it was sold for £250.» Which number is the valuation? | *£400, the expert's view of what it is worth | The vase | £250, the day it was sold | The old shop
test: «Ravi asked an expert for a valuation of his grandad's watch.» What does Ravi want to know? | Where to buy a new strap | How old the watch is in years | How to tell the time | *How much an expert thinks the watch is worth
test: «The class gave her a high valuation for being kind.» What does high valuation mean here? | She was the fastest runner | She has a very loud voice | *The class thinks she is very valuable to them
exam: Which sentence is about a valuation rather than a price? | «The shop sold the bike for £80.» | *«The expert said the bike was worth about £120.» | «The sweets cost 50p each.» | «Mum paid £5 for the milk.»
